-- title:
--   Exact original BV strict physical-row cash and survival-terminal payoff is bounded on immediate ruin
-- statement:
--   For the original infinite-activity bounded-variation spectrally negative Levy process, admissible dividend strategy and arbitrary supplied physical uniform grid/spatial bands exactly as BVA63, take its literal strict cash F_m and survival-at-T terminal term. At every path with ruinTime=0, the survival terminal vanishes and F_m≤w(x) for every row m, using the proven original strict-horizon initial-ruin Stieltjes cash inequality. The strict cash cut-off T−T/(m+2)>0 is verified arithmetically. This disposes of the zero-ruin component of BVA63's actual pathwise ledger, leaving the positive ruin clock case and compensated source N.

